# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Settings of the demo stack itself. Copy to .env in this directory; every
# value below is the default the compose file already uses, so an untouched
# copy changes nothing.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# These are compose variables, not the application's. The full registry of
# AICC_* settings is the repository's .env.example.

# --- what the AI leg talks to -------------------------------------------------
# One provider answers every call, chosen here (phase1-decisions A1): qwen
# inside mainland China, openai elsewhere. Without its key the screens, the
# history and the human path all work; only the bot cannot speak.
#AICC_PROVIDER=openai
#OPENAI_API_KEY=
#ALIYUN_API_KEY=
#AICC_PROVIDER_ENDPOINT=
#AICC_PROVIDER_MODEL=

# --- the demo dataset ---------------------------------------------------------
# demo seeds a team, two queues, a published bilingual flow behind 95001/95002
# and seven days of history. fresh removes all of that again — the way back to
# an empty product once the volume exists. Empty leaves the database alone.
#AICC_SEED=demo

# --- where it listens ---------------------------------------------------------
# Loopback by default: the demo ships documented passwords and must not face a
# network. 0.0.0.0 opens it to the LAN, knowingly.
#HTTP_BIND=127.0.0.1
#SIP_BIND=127.0.0.1

# --- a softphone outside this machine -----------------------------------------
# Set to the host's LAN address and uncomment the RTP range in the compose file
# to register a real phone and hear audio. Empty keeps the demo self-contained,
# which is enough for AI calls: they never leave the compose network.
#FS_EXTERNAL_IP=

# --- which switch image ------------------------------------------------------
# The switch is this repository's own image, built by freeswitch/build.sh from
# freeswitch/. Point this at a locally built one to try a change to that tree
# before it is pushed: `make fs-image` builds aicc-freeswitch:v1.11.3 for this
# machine's architecture.
#
# Sound files are in the image now, at 8 kHz, so there is nothing to download
# at first boot any more. An image built with SOUNDS=none has no queue hold
# music and nothing else changes.
#AICC_FS_IMAGE=rasonyang/freeswitch-aicc:v1.11.3

# --- live transcription of the human phase ------------------------------------
# The switch image carries mod_audio_stream, so this is possible in the demo.
# It is off because it also needs a recogniser credential and the stream
# settings — see the repository root .env.example, which is the registry for
# every AICC_ setting. A switch told to transcribe without the module refuses
# to start rather than tapping nothing in silence.
#AICC_TRANSCRIPTION_ENABLED=false

# --- credentials of the stack -------------------------------------------------
# Fine as they are on a laptop. Change all three anywhere else.
#POSTGRES_PASSWORD=aicc
#LUA_PASSWORD=aicc-lua
#ESL_PASSWORD=ClueCon

# The switch's own domain. Queue names are rendered with it on both sides and
# mod_callcenter matches them literally, so the two containers are configured
# from this one value.
#SWITCH_DOMAIN=aicc.demo

# --- the image ----------------------------------------------------------------
# By default compose builds the application from this checkout. Point AICC_IMAGE
# at a published tag to skip the build entirely.
#AICC_IMAGE=ghcr.io/rasonyang/ai-native-callcenter:latest
#AICC_VERSION=demo
#AICC_LOG_LEVEL=info
